[38;2;184;134;11m    - records the violation, the evidence and the rule in `docs/SLAPS.md` (permanent ledger),[0m
[38;2;184;134;11m    - appends the rule to this file,[0m
[38;2;255;255;255;48;2;119;20;20m-   - **dispatches a correction order into the offending bot's own chat**, so the bot takes a turn and[0m
[38;2;255;255;255;48;2;119;20;20m-     has to fix the defect and answer for it with real output,[0m
[38;2;255;255;255;48;2;19;87;20m+   - **dispatches a correction order into the offending bot's own chat**, so the bot takes a turn and has to fix the defect and answer for it with real output,[0m
[38;2;184;134;11m    - re-runs the acceptance command and records whether the fix actually verified.[0m
[38;2;184;134;11m 4. **Escalation ladder** (automatic, by repeat count of the same rule):[0m
[38;2;184;134;11m    - **Level 1 — warning.** Fix it and reply with evidence.[0m
[38;2;255;255;255;48;2;119;20;20m-   - **Level 2 — the rule is written into that bot's `SOUL.md`.** It now loads in every session that[0m
[38;2;255;255;255;48;2;119;20;20m-     bot ever runs, forever. This is the part that stops repeat mistakes.[0m
[38;2;255;255;255;48;2;119;20;20m-   - **Level 3 — the lane is frozen.** `forge` must reassign the work; the frozen bot may only run[0m
